<title>DUBAI: Iran oil processing deal in Yemen delayed.</title>
<headline>Iran oil processing deal in Yemen delayed.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A deal for Iranian oil to start being processed at Yemen's Aden refinery this month has been delayed as price negotiations continue, Yemeni oil officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The processing has not yet begun...It was supposed to start in September but a delegation will go to Iran to finalise aspects of the deal shortly,&quot; an official in Sanaa said.</p>
<p>Iran had been expected to start processing 15,000 barrels per day (bpd) of its crude at the Aden refinery this month as part of broader energy cooperation between the two states.</p>
<p>Officials could not say when Aden would receive its first shipment of Iranian crude for processing.</p>
<p>-- Dubai Newsroom +971 4 6071255</p>
</text>
